%T A398257 55900863338506060256,3359695883345876427856640,
%U A398257 717046883510705337814399971200,552177043831717222237029917934822912,1552304317212511130749960011067429932294784
%N A398257 Number of unlabeled digraphs with n nodes containing a global source and a global sink, self-loops allowed.
%C A398257 Self-loops on the source or sink are impossible (a loop gives nonzero in-/out-degree), so loops occur on the other n-2 nodes only.
%C A398257 Loops-allowed analog of A350794, as A351052 is of A350360.
%D A398257 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%F A398257 R. W. Robinson's Eqn 21 applied to digraphs with self-loop edges: x - x^2 + Euler(S)*(x*exp(-S) X x*exp(-S) X D).
%o A398257 (PARI) \\ See PARI link in A350794 for program code.
%o A398257 A398257seq(n)={Vec(InitFinallyV(GraphCIData(n, DigraphWithLoopEdges)))}
%o A398257 A398257seq(14)
%Y A398257 Cf. A350794, A351052, A350796.
%K A398257 nonn
%O A398257 1,3
%A A398257 _Gregory Morse_, Jul 24 2026
